    <string name="ussd_automation_guide">How to Build a USSD Flow</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">How to create and execute USSD Automations step-by-step:</string>
    <string name="guide_step1">1. Dial Shortcode (e.g., *170#): Opens your network operator\'s main USSD menu.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2">2. Automated Menu Selection (e.g., Option 1): Automatically enters a numeric menu option (for example, \'1\' for Transfer or \'2\' for Airtime).</string>
    <string name="guide_step3">3. Manual (Menu Selection): Pauses execution to allow manual interaction or selecting menu choices directly on screen.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4">4. Dynamic User Input: Prompts for recipient phone numbers, transaction amounts, or custom reference details when running the flow.</string>
    <string name="guide_step5">5. Secure PIN Input: Automatically or securely handles PIN entries for authorization during transfers.</string>
